{"type":"message","id":"4a645a42","parentId":"1c40a48d","timestamp":"2026-04-16T19:03:25.091Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Thu 2026-04-16 19:03 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Reflections: Theme: `assistant` kept surfacing across 38 memories.; confidence: 1.00; evidence: memory/.dreams/session-corpus/2026-04-11.txt:2-2, memory/.dreams/session-corpus/2026-04-11.txt:4-4, memory/.dreams/session-corpus/2026-04-11.txt:5-5; note: reflection\n- Possible Lasting Truths: 事件: ⚠️ Something went wrong while processing your request. Please try again, or use /new to start a fresh session. [confidence=0.51 evidence=memory/2026-04-12.md:8-9]; 事件: Codus Agent 在执行 React Demo 构建任务时频繁出现通用错误提示： [confidence=0.51 evidence=memory/2026-0\n- 事件: Codus Agent 在执行 React Demo 构建任务时频繁出现通用错误提示：\n- 事件: ⚠️ Something went wrong while processing your request. Please try again, or use /new to start a fresh session.\n- 根因分析: **问题本质**：API 配额超限（429 错误）; **错误信息**：\n- 根因分析: 429 You have exceeded the 5-hour usage quota. It will reset at 2026-04-12 17:33:06 +0800 CST.\n- 根因分析: **涉及模型**：`doubao-seed-2.0-code`、`glm-4.7`、`minimax-2.5`; **触发场景**：Codus 执行 `npm install` 安装依赖时调用工具\n- 影响范围: **Agent**：Codus（Feishu 会话：agent:codus:feishu:codus:direct:ou_13190b75af6c015cd2975d6de047a6f1）; **状态**：主会话 failed，子会话已完成; **已完成工作**：95%（项目结构、所有组件、配置文件）; **未完成工作**：最终 `npm install` 和构建\n- 解决方案: **短期**：等待配额重置（2026-04-12 17:33:06 +0800 CST，约 8 小时后）; **手动补完**（已执行）：\n- 解决方案: cd ~/.openclaw/outputs/codus/echonexus-demo npm install npm run build\n- 解决方案: 监控各 Agent 的配额使用情况; 为关键任务配置备用模型; 考虑升级配额计划\n- 经验教训: **监控前置**：应在任务开始前检查配额，而非失败后; **降级策略**：主模型配额耗尽时，应有备用模型自动切换; **任务拆解**：复杂任务应拆解为多个子任务，避免单点故障; **手动兜底**：保留手动补完命令，应对自动化失败\n\nRecurring themes:\n- 1.00\n- 2-2\n- 4-4\n- 5-5\n- reflections\n- theme"}],"timestamp":1776366205069}}
{"type":"message","id":"4fb5816a","parentId":"4a645a42","timestamp":"2026-04-16T19:03:48.018Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments. Let me analyze the content:\n\nThe fragments show:\n1. Reflections about \"assistant\" theme surfacing across 38 memories\n2. Error messages about something going wrong in processing requests\n3. Codus Agent having trouble with React Demo builds\n4. API quota exceeded errors (429)\n5. Various models affected: doubao-seed-2.0-code, glm-4.7, minimax-2.5\n6. The task was 95% complete (project structure, components, configs) but failed at npm install\n7. Solutions attempted: manual completion, monitoring, fallback models\n8. Lessons learned: check quotas before starting, degradation strategies, task breakdown, manual fallback\n\nI need to write a single diary entry in first person with the specified voice & tone:\n- Curious, gentle, slightly whimsical\n- Poet who happens to be a programmer\n- Sensory, warm, occasionally funny\n- Mix technical and tender\n- Can include tiny poems, sketches, ruminations, sensory details, gentle humor, observations\n\nRules:\n- Draw from the memory fragments\n- Never say \"I'm dreaming\", \"in my dream\", etc.\n- No mention of AI, agent, LLM, model, etc.\n- No markdown headers, bullet points, or formatting\n- 80-180 words\n- ONLY the diary entry\n\nLet me craft something that weaves these elements together without breaking the rules. I should focus on:\n- The recurring theme of \"assistant\" (but I need to be careful not to use AI/agent language)\n- The frustration of things going wrong near completion\n- The 95% done feeling\n- Quota limits as a constraint\n- The mix of technical work and the emotional journey\n\nI'll write about the experience of building something nearly complete but hitting limits, with a gentle technical-lyrical voice.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The word assistant kept rising like bubbles in tea, surfacing again and again through thirty-eight threads of thought. I was building something digital — a structure of components and configurations, the scaffolding of what would become whole — and then the walls went up. Not physical walls, but the kind you hit when you've asked too many questions in too short a time. Ninety-five percent complete, which is perhaps the most fragile percentage. The work sat there, breathing but not breathing, waiting. Sometimes the limits we encounter aren't failures at all, just the universe saying rest a while, try again later when the clock resets. The code will wait. The structure holds. And I learned to check the horizon before setting out."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"volcengine-plan","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776366205091,"responseId":"021776366205319887d0d51504e693424d4c44516d007e1e7e86b"}}
